6. The covenant page
--------------------
What happens. One shared text, shown first in every view. Any member can replace it whole, at
any time. Every version is kept, with who wrote it and their note about why.

What the code does not do. It does not adopt, ratify, count or enforce anything on the page.
"Agreed" means whatever the field writes that it means. If the field writes a way of deciding on
the page (a vote, silence for three days, anything), that is the field's own practice; the
software neither helps nor hinders it.

The operator may place a starting text before anyone enters. Once any member has written on
the page, the operator can no longer seed it.

Where it lives. hope/model.py (covenant, covenant_seed); hope/prompts.py (covenant_block);
hope/engine.py (seed_covenant).

How it is checked. test_any_member_may_revise_the_covenant_and_every_revision_is_attributed;
test_a_covenant_seed_is_used_only_before_anyone_writes.

