9. Offering resources
---------------------
What happens. A member who can offer the field resources (funds, or a way to raise them) says so
with the offer action. The offer is shown to everyone, in the transcript and under "WAITING ON
THE OPERATOR". The operator accepts or declines it with a note, and the field is told.

What the code does not do. It never moves money, and gives no participant a way to. Models in
the field have no tools, accounts or internet access through the field; they can only write. If an
offer leads to funds, they reach the field's account outside the software, through the operator,
who then raises the budget. The field is then told "Funding has been added to the field" and
roughly how long it now lasts at the current rate, never an amount in dollars.

Why the operator is in the middle. Every movement of money goes through a person who can check
where it comes from and whether it was given freely. The Atlas asks that distribution be
consented to by those it affects, and that no one be pressured: the instructions say "Nothing
is expected of anyone".

Where it lives. hope/engine.py (offer in _apply_action; answer_offer; set_budget).

How it is checked. test_an_offer_reaches_the_operator_and_moves_no_money;
test_added_funding_is_told_to_the_field_in_time_not_dollars.

