12. Leaving, coming back, and where words may go
------------------------------------------------
What happens. Any member may withdraw at any moment, with or without a reason, and may say when
it would be fair to ask them back. It takes effect immediately. What they said stays in the
transcript. A member who has left is not asked again unless they come back.

Coming back. Leaving is not final. Someone who has left may be asked back: at their own request
(a person holding a seat link sees "Ask to return" on their seat page once they have left), or
by the operator (the console's Ask back, or the reinvite command), in keeping with the terms
they gave. A former member is asked the entry question again, beside everything else, so a
running field need not stop for them; the question opens with how they left, the terms they gave, and
why they are asked now. Someone who declined is asked the invitation again, at the next Open, in
the same way. Either way they answer like anyone else, and no is as complete an answer as
before. A yes is recorded as their return ("returned"), and everything they said before is
still theirs.

When the operator closes a field for good, they may ask each member with a seat one question:
may your contributions be shown to a later field? A member may say all, only the entries they
name, or none: on a seat page, three buttons; at a terminal, "share", "share #12 #15", or "no".
Anything else is handed back as not an answer. Silence is none. Only a member's own entries can
be named. A later field can then carry only those entries, reachable by recall, with their
authors named and not present.

Where it lives. hope/model.py (withdraw, reinvite); hope/engine.py (reinvite, _ask_returners,
